---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ChatWidget from '../components/ChatWidget.astro';

const trades = [
  "Painters", "Roofers", "HVAC", "Plumbers", "Electricians", "Concrete",
  "Landscapers", "Remodelers", "Junk removal", "Pest control",
  "Cleaning companies", "Hair salons",
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Can an AI assistant answer calls for a painting company?",
    a: "Yes. An AI assistant can answer a painting company's phone, greet the caller by the business name, ask what kind of job they need, take down their name, number, and address, and text you the details before you've finished the wall you're standing on. There are two versions of this. The simpler one answers, takes a message out loud, and sends you a text with who called and why, so you decide whether it's worth calling back. The fuller one qualifies the caller and books the estimate straight into your calendar. Painting is a good fit for either one because most of your calls come in while your hands are occupied and a homeowner planning a repaint will call three painters in a row. The one who answers is usually the one who gets the walkthrough. If nobody answers, the job is gone before you've wiped your hands.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is an AI receptionist for a contractor?",
    a: "An AI receptionist is a phone system that picks up when you can't, holds a real conversation with the caller, and turns that call into something you can act on. It answers in your business name, asks the questions you would ask, and either takes a message or books the appointment. It works nights, weekends, and the middle of a job. The difference between an AI receptionist and voicemail is that voicemail asks the customer to do the work and most of them won't. The difference between an AI receptionist and a hired receptionist is cost and hours: a person costs a salary and works part of the day, and an AI answers every call at any hour for a fraction of that. For a one truck operation or a small crew, it's usually the first hire you can afford.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can AI book appointments for a roofing company?",
    a: "Yes. An AI receptionist can be connected directly to your calendar, so when a homeowner calls about a leak or a roof inspection, the assistant checks your real availability and books the slot while the caller is still on the phone. The booking shows up on your calendar and both of you get a confirmation. This matters more in roofing than in most trades because roofing calls arrive in bursts. A storm comes through and forty people call the same afternoon. Without something answering, most of those calls hit voicemail and the homeowner moves down the list. With booking connected, the calls that come in while you're on a roof are already on your schedule by the time you're back on the ground.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should a plumber put a chatbot on their website?",
    a: "It's worth it if your website already gets visitors, and it's not worth much if it doesn't. A chatbot on a plumbing website answers the questions people ask before they call: do you handle water heaters, do you come out at night, what areas do you cover, how fast can somebody get here. It answers in your voice, using your real service list and service area, and it can hand the visitor straight into booking a call. The honest version of this answer is that a chatbot is a conversion tool, not a traffic tool. It helps the people who already found you decide to contact you. If almost nobody is landing on your website yet, fixing that comes first and the chat widget can wait. The chat widget on this website is the same one I install, so you can open it and see exactly how it behaves before you decide.",
  },
  {
    q: "What happens when I miss a call if I have missed call text back?",
    a: "The moment a call goes unanswered, the caller automatically gets a text from your business number saying you missed them and asking what they need. At the same time you get a text telling you who called. When they reply, their answer comes to you and you can text back and forth normally. Nothing about it feels automated to the customer, and they get a response in seconds instead of wondering whether they picked the wrong company. This is the simplest piece of the whole system and usually the one that pays for itself first, because a missed call with no follow up is a customer who is already dialing your competitor. It also requires no change to your phone, your number, or how you work. I offer this one as a free two week trial precisely because the results are easy to see: you count the replies.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need a new website to use an AI assistant?",
    a: "No. The phone side works on the number you already have, whatever your website situation is. Missed call text back, the AI message taker, and the AI receptionist all attach to your existing business line, so you can run any of them without touching your website at all. The website chatbot is the one exception, since it needs a website to live on, but it can be added to most existing sites without rebuilding them. Where a new website does help is everything upstream of the call: if people can't find you on Google in the first place, a perfect phone system has nothing to answer. If you want both, they get built together. If you only want the phone piece, that's a real option and often the faster way to see whether any of this is worth your money.",
  },
  {
    q: "Will my customers know they are talking to an AI?",
    a: "Some will and some won't, and I don't recommend hiding it. The assistant introduces itself by name and speaks naturally, and most callers treat it exactly like a receptionist. If a caller asks directly whether they're speaking with a person, it tells them the truth. That's a deliberate choice. A customer who finds out later that they were deceived on the first call has learned something about your business that no amount of good work undoes, and in a trade that runs on referrals that's a bad trade for a slightly smoother phone call. What customers actually care about is that somebody picked up, understood what they needed, and got them on the schedule. That's what this delivers.",
  },
  {
    q: "How much does an AI assistant for a contractor cost?",
    a: "It depends on which pieces you want and how much call volume you have, so I price it after a call rather than putting a number on a page that may not fit your business. What moves the number is straightforward: whether you want text back only or a full voice assistant, whether it books into a calendar or just takes messages, how many calls a month it handles, and whether a website or chat widget is part of the project. What I can tell you without a call is where to start. Missed call text back is the cheapest and fastest piece to put in, it takes about a day, and I run it as a free two week trial so you can see real numbers on your own phone before any money changes hands. Most people should start there and add the rest once they've watched it work.",
  },
];

const products = [
  {
    title: "Missed Call Text Back",
    body: "Every call you miss gets an instant text from your number asking what they need, and you get told who called. Free for the first two weeks so you can count the replies yourself.",
    href: "/missed-call-text-back/",
    linkText: "How missed call text back works",
  },
  {
    title: "AI Message Taker",
    body: "A voice assistant answers the calls you miss, has a real conversation, takes down the details out loud, and texts you who called and why.",
  },
  {
    title: "AI Receptionist",
    body: "The full version. It answers in your business name, asks your qualifying questions, checks your calendar, and books the estimate while the caller is still on the phone.",
  },
  {
    title: "Website Chat",
    body: "A chat widget that answers questions in your voice using your real services and service area, then hands the visitor into booking. The one on this page is the same one I install.",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="AI Assistant for Contractors That Answers Every Call"
  description="AI receptionists, missed call text back, and website chat for painters, roofers, HVAC, plumbers, and local trades. Answer every call and book more jobs. Built in the USA."
  ogImage="https://reynahouse.ai/images/rhai_og.png"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Service",
      "name": "AI Assistants for Contractors and Local Trades",
      "serviceType": "AI receptionist and call answering for contractors",
      "provider": { "@id": "https://reynahouse.ai/#org" },
      "areaServed": ["United States"],
      "description": "AI receptionists, AI message taking, missed call text back, and website chat for contractors and local trades. Answers the calls a business misses, qualifies the caller, and books the job into a calendar.",
      "url": "https://reynahouse.ai/ai-for-contractors/",
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": f.q,
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a },
      })),
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://reynahouse.ai/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Local Service Businesses", "item": "https://reynahouse.ai/websites-for-local-service-businesses/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "AI for Contractors", "item": "https://reynahouse.ai/ai-for-contractors/" },
      ],
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <Header />

  <main class="page">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <article class="intro">
      <div class="intro__container">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> <a href="/websites-for-local-service-businesses/">Local Service Businesses</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> AI for Contractors
        </nav>
        <span class="overline">BUILT FOR CONTRACTORS AND TRADES</span>
        <h1 class="h1">AI Assistant for Contractors and Local Trades</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          The average contractor misses a lot of calls, and most of those callers
          never leave a voicemail. They just dial the next number on the list.
          Every one of those was a job you already earned by showing up in the
          search, and you lost it because your hands were busy.
        </p>
        <p class="body body--gold">
          An AI assistant answers when you can't. It takes the call, gets the
          details, and either texts you who called or books the job straight into
          your calendar. Nights, weekends, and the middle of a job.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- THE FOUR PIECES -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section__container">
        <h2 class="h2">What an AI Assistant Actually Does</h2>
        <p class="body">
          This isn't one product. It's four, and most businesses start with one
          and add the rest later. You can run any of them on the phone number you
          already have.
        </p>
        <div class="cards">
          {products.map((p) => (
            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="card__title">{p.title}</h3>
              <p class="card__body">{p.body}</p>
              {p.href && <a class="inline-link card__link" href={p.href}>{p.linkText} &rarr;</a>}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- THE MATH -->
    <section class="section section--tint">
      <div class="section__container">
        <h2 class="h2">Why a Missed Call Costs More Than You Think</h2>
        <p class="body">
          A homeowner with a leak, a dead furnace, or a peeling exterior does not
          call one contractor. They work down the search results until somebody
          picks up. The first business to answer is the one that gets to quote,
          and the quote usually decides the job.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          That means the call you missed at 2pm wasn't a lost lead. It was a lost
          job, handed to whoever was second on the list. And it happened after you
          already paid for the website, the listing, and the search ranking that
          made the phone ring in the first place.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          Answering is the cheapest part of the whole funnel and it's the part
          most trades leave to voicemail.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HONESTY / PROOF -->
    <section class="section section--dark">
      <div class="section__container">
        <span class="overline overline--light">HOW I KNOW THIS WORKS</span>
        <h2 class="h2 h2--light">I Run All of It on My Own Business First</h2>
        <p class="body body--light">
          I'm not going to tell you what other contractors are getting, because I
          build websites and automation for local businesses and I'm honest about
          where my track record is. What I can show you is my own setup.
        </p>
        <p class="body body--light">
          The missed call system runs on my business line right now. The chat
          widget on this page is the same one I put on client sites; open it and
          ask it something. The AI receptionist is live and takes real calls. I
          don't sell a tool I haven't run on my own phone through a full week of
          being too busy to answer it.
        </p>
        <p class="body body--light">
          Everything here is built in the United States, by me, and you own your
          setup. No overseas team, no locked platform, no monthly ransom to keep
          your own phone system running.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHO IT'S FOR -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section__container">
        <h2 class="h2">Who This Is For</h2>
        <div class="trades">
          {trades.map((t) => <span class="trade">{t}</span>)}
        </div>
        <p class="body trades__note">
          The pattern is the same in every trade: the work happens with your hands
          full, the calls come in anyway, and the customer who doesn't get an
          answer calls somebody else. If that describes your week, this fixes it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
    <section class="section section--tint">
      <div class="section__container">
        <h2 class="h2">How It Works</h2>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Start With the Free Two Weeks</h3>
            <p>Missed call text back goes on your existing number, usually in a day. No contract, no card, nothing changes about how you work.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Count What It Catches</h3>
            <p>At the end of two weeks you look at your own phone and see how many callers replied who would have been a voicemail. That's the whole pitch.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <h3>Add the Rest When You're Ready</h3>
            <p>If the numbers are worth it, we add voice answering, calendar booking, or website chat. If they aren't, you keep the two weeks and we shake hands.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="section section--cta">
      <div class="section__container">
        <h2 class="h2">Stop Losing Jobs to Voicemail</h2>
        <p class="body">
          Tell me your trade and roughly how many calls you miss in a week, and
          I'll tell you which piece to start with. Book a free call; no pressure,
          no obligation.
        </p>
        <div class="cta__actions">
          <a href="/#contact" class="btn btn--primary">Book a Free Call &rarr;</a>
          <a href="tel:+19093410243" class="btn btn--ghost">Or call 909-341-0243</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section section--tint">
      <div class="section__container section__container--narrow">
        <h2 class="h2">Common Questions About AI for Contractors</h2>
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="faq">
            <summary class="faq__q">{f.q}</summary>
            <p class="faq__a">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- RELATED -->
    <section class="related">
      <div class="related__container">
        <p class="related__title">Keep Reading</p>
        <div class="related__grid">
          <a class="related__card" href="/missed-call-text-back/">
            <span>Missed Call Text Back</span>
            <small>The free two week trial, explained start to finish.</small>
          </a>
          <a class="related__card" href="/websites-for-contractors/">
            <span>Websites for Contractors</span>
            <small>The site that makes the phone ring in the first place.</small>
          </a>
          <a class="related__card" href="/why-not-showing-on-google/">
            <span>Why Isn't My Business on Google?</span>
            <small>The usual reasons, and how to fix them.</small>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <ChatWidget />
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .page { background-color: var(--white); }
  .intro { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--navy) 0%, #1a1a2e 100%); padding: 72px 24px 64px; }
  .intro__container { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .crumbs { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--tan); margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .crumbs a { color: var(--copper-light); }
  .crumbs a:hover { color: var(--copper); }
  .overline { display: block; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; color: var(--copper-light); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-size: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .h1 { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; color: var(--white); font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.05; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .lede { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: var(--white); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .section { padding: 64px 24px; }
  .section--tint { background-color: var(--cream); }
  .section--dark { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--forest) 0%, #1a2a1c 100%); }
  .section--cta { background-color: var(--white); text-align: center; }
  .section__container { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .section__container--narrow { max-width: 760px; }
  .h2 { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; color: var(--navy); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4.5vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .h2--light { color: var(--white); }
  .body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: var(--dark); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .body--light { color: var(--cream); }
  .body--gold { color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600; }
  .inline-link { color: var(--copper-dark); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .inline-link:hover { color: var(--copper); }

  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 20px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--tan); border-radius: 10px; padding: 24px; }
  .card__title { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; color: var(--navy); font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.02em; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.1; }
  .card__body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: var(--dark); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .card__link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .trades { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .trade { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--navy); background: var(--cream); border: 1px solid var(--tan); border-radius: 999px; padding: 8px 16px; }
  .trades__note { margin-top: 28px; }

  .steps { display: grid; gap: 16px; margin-top: 28px; counter-reset: step; }
  .step { position: relative; padding: 20px 20px 20px 68px; background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--tan); border-radius: 10px; }
  .step::before { counter-increment: step; content: counter(step); position: absolute; left: 20px; top: 20px; width: 34px; height: 34px; display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--copper); color: var(--white); font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 1.25rem; border-radius: 50%; }
  .step h3 { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .step p { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: var(--dark); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .cta__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; justify-content: center; margin-top: 28px; }
  .btn { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1rem; padding: 14px 26px; border-radius: 8px; transition: background-color 0.2s ease, color 0.2s ease; }
  .btn--primary { background-color: var(--copper); color: var(--white); }
  .btn--primary:hover { background-color: #b8843f; }
  .btn--ghost { border: 1px solid var(--navy); color: var(--navy); }
  .btn--ghost:hover { background-color: var(--navy); color: var(--white); }
  .btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--copper); outline-offset: 2px; }

  .faq { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tan); padding: 16px 0; }
  .faq__q { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; color: var(--copper-dark); font-size: 0.95rem; cursor: pointer; list-style: none; padding: 4px 0; }
  .faq__q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq__q::before { content: '+ '; font-weight: 700; }
  details[open] .faq__q::before { content: '− '; }
  .faq__a { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: var(--navy); font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.7; padding: 12px 0 4px; }

  .related { background: var(--cream); padding: 48px 24px; }
  .related__container { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .related__title { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; color: var(--copper-dark); font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .related__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .related__card { display: block; background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--tan); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px; transition: border-color 0.2s ease; }
  .related__card:hover { border-color: var(--copper); }
  .related__card span { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  .related__card small { display: block; font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; color: var(--dark); font-size: 0.85rem; margin-top: 6px; line-height: 1.5; }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .related__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
